The method used to approximate the equilibrium point was to determine the root of the curve displayed in Figure \ref{fig: g=0}, approximate the value of $x$, and insert this value into Equation (\ref{Eq: 5}) to approximate the value of $y$ at the equilibrium point. This process is depicted in Figure \ref{fig: root}, where the equilibrium point (accurate to ten significant figures) is: \[ [CDK1] = 0.4485197689 \text{ and } [APC] = 0.4698435624. \]

