For an exponential population model,
\[ \frac{dF}{dt} = rF, \]
where $r$ represents the growth rate of the population, the solution is given by
\[ F(t) = F_0e^{rt}. \]

The doubling time of the population $\tau_2$ is the time it takes for the population to double in size. Therefore,

\begin{align}
