\section{Fast-VGAN Voice Conversion}
\label{sec:proposed_method}

In this section, we detail the rationale behind our architectural choices. Our goal is to design a model capable of transferring a specific utterance from one speaker to another speaker’s timbre, while relying on high-level control features. To facilitate training on limited data and ensure a lightweight implementation, we impose constraints on the model’s parameter count and structural complexity. We introduce Fast-VGAN, a lightweight architecture designed to resynthesize mel-spectrograms from interpretable conditioning inputs, including F0, intensity, phoneme sequence, and speaker identity. We describe the methodology used to extract and process these conditioning features.


