Proteins are complex three-dimensional structures composed of hundreds to thousands of atoms, arranged in a specific manner in space. These molecular architectures as well as their dynamic fluctuations are crucial for the function of a protein.
%Local protein structure plays a central role in determining a protein's function and its interactions within complex biomolecular environments. 
