\title{Absoluteness of Fixed Points}



\begin{abstract}
We characterize those complete commutative positive linear ordered monoids $\cW$ such that whenever $f$ is a map from a Cauchy complete $\cW$-metric space to itself, the existence of a fixed point of $f$ is independent of the background model of set theory. 
\end{abstract}

