\section{Future Work}
%%%% %%%% %%%% %%%% %%%% %%%% %%%% %%%% 
We end with a couple of directions for future work. 
\begin{itemize}
\item[(Q1)] For which, not necessarily linear, quantales $\cW$ is having a fixed point absolute for all $\cW$-dynamical systems? (where here we are replacing distance monoids with quantales in the obvious way).

\item[(Q2)] For a fixed $\cW$, is there a characterization of those $\cW$-dynamical systems for which having a fixed point is not absolute?
\end{itemize}

