\subsection{Threshold edge-drive amplitudes}

We compute the steady-state solutions of the damped driven discrete nonlinear Schr\"odinger equation, as described in Subsection \ref{subsec:analysis_numerics}, for $\Omega \in [0.01, 3]$. Our goal is to identify the critical edge thresholds $A_c^\pm$.  The calculations use the parameters $F = 0.00027$ and $\Gamma = 0$. The numerical results are compared with the analytical predictions for the turning points derived in Subsections \ref{subsec:analysis_Omega_less1} and \ref{subsec:analysis_Omega_great1}. This comparison is presented in Fig.\ \ref{fig:Om_Ac}. As expected, the Barashenkov-Bogdanov-Zhalan soliton model \eqref{eq:Ac_small} shows good agreement with the numerical simulations for $\Omega \ll 1$, although it slightly underestimates the critical edge drive. This deviation becomes more noticeable as $\Omega \to 1$. The approximation \eqref{eq:Ac_large} also agrees well with the numerical results $A_c^\pm$ for $\Omega \gg 1$. This demonstrates the overall accuracy of the turning point calculations derived from both analytical approximations.

