	\subsection{From Vietoris-Rips thickenings to persistence modules.}

	The following proposition is a generalization of the first inequality in \cite[Theorem A]{adams2024persistent} to the $G$-equivariant setting.

	\begin{proposition}\label{prop:GdHTGdI}
		For any two filtered $G$-topological spaces $(X,\alpha_X,\beta_X)$ and $(Y,\alpha_Y,\beta_Y)$ and for all integers $k\geq 0$, we have that
		$$\dht^G(X,Y)\geq\di^G\big(\h_k(\beta_X^{-1}(-\infty,\bullet)),\h_k(\beta_Y^{-1}(-\infty,\bullet))\big).$$
	\end{proposition}

