\begin{cor} \label{cor:3h_SingIdeals}
    The ideal $\SSS_K(\GGG_{3S})$ is not $S$-simple if and only if there exists $b \in K$ such that $\Delta_b = 0_K$. 

    In that case, $\langle [1,b,-(b+1)] \rangle$ is a singular ideal of $\AAA_K(\GGG_{3S})$. 
\end{cor}

