\caption{(a) The contour integral when calculating the wave function from $\psi_p$. The red point means the complex poles of $\psi_p$,  contributing an exact bound state. (b) Real poles along the real axis for an extended (or non-normalizable) wave function. (c) The dispersion relation of the $\delta$ function potential system. The energy of the bound state ($E_{\text{b}}$) and the associated wave function are shown. (d) The energy of the extended case. The red point indicates the momentum (or pole) of the wave function. }
