	\subsection{Backreaction and Saturation}

	The sustained amplification described in the previous section provides a powerful mechanism for transferring energy from the $\phi$ cloud to the $\chi$ ring. This process, however, cannot continue indefinitely. As the $\chi$ ring grows in mass and density, its backreaction on the primary $\phi$ cloud becomes significant, eventually halting the energy transfer. In this section, we analyze this backreaction process to determine the final, saturated state of the system.

