\label{fig:accountsreached}
\end{figure}

Over 35\% of the accounts that have been exposed to our content choose to view it. Figure \ref{fig:accountsreached} (top) illustrates both the impressions and accounts reached. On Instagram, 'impressions' refer to the number of times our content has been displayed to users, meaning the total number of opportunities for an account to see a video, post, or account (e.g., through the search feed). 'Accounts reached' represents the number of accounts that, after being prompted by Instagram, actually decided to view the content. However, this does not guarantee that they watched the videos in their entirety or interacted with them.


