%% Comparing to Lazification
\cref{fig:lazy_solved_instances,fig:lazy_dual_gaps} showcase the performance of the lazified versions of the methods (there applicable).
We can cleary observe that lazification has a positive impact if the LMO of the corresponding problem is computionally expensive as is the case for the Spectrahedron, the Nuclear Norm Ball, the Poisson Problem and most noteably the $K$-Sparse Polytope.
It should be pointed out that the Poisson Problem was modelled using \texttt{MathOptInterface.jl}, hence the LMO performed by an LP solver instead of a specialised routine.

