\section{Introduction}

The Reidemeister theorem is one of the most foundational and classical results in knot theory \cite{reidemeister}. It states that two diagrams $D,D' \subset \R^2$ of unoriented, unframed links in $\R^3$   are isotopic if and only if they are related by a sequence of planar isotopies and the so-called \textit{Reidemeister moves} $\Omega 1$, $\Omega 2$ and $\Omega 3$ depicted below:
\begin{equation}\label{eq:unfr_unor_Rmoves}
