    \label{photo}
\end{figure}

The experiment was carried out under laboratory conditions. Initially, the prototype took off from a platform at the same height as the water surface($z=0$) and ascended to an altitude of 0.5$m$ above the water. Subsequently, it dived into the water and reached a depth of -0.5$m$. Finally, the prototype ascended, crossed back over the water surface, and returned to an elevation of 0.5 m.

